    help_body: "claude -p runs once as a user session (your default model) and once as an agent session (haiku) in an empty folder, so only the load the global harness adds to every session is measured. Time is split using the debug log: local startup (settings, plugins, hooks, local MCP — the only part the harness controls), network wait (remote requests such as account settings and connectors), headless plugin check (claude -p only), API response wait (server speed), and answer & exit (output length). Any segment more than 0.5 s slower than the baseline gets the cause found in the log. Each probe runs once, so network and server segments are expected to fluctuate. Savings are not the billed difference but ‘base tokens removed × the baseline's cost per token’ — back-to-back runs warm the cache and make billed costs look lower than they really are.",
